id: pm-gtw5zh
title: Metadata index rebuilds and mutations repeatedly scan an unindexed FTS identity column
description: "The 100000-item explicit child-read scale control spends minutes rebuilding the optional SQLite projection. A five-second CPU profile attributed 4588 of 4618 samples to SQLite statement execution. insertRow deletes item_search WHERE id for every row although id is UNINDEXED in FTS5, causing a growing full-table scan during rebuild and O(n) individual mutations. Bind FTS rowid to the indexed items identity lookup, preserve update/delete/search parity and invalidate older derived schemas."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T10:04:49.937Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T11:20:08.570Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T11:14:19.182Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T11:14:19.182Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: FTS maintenance uses indexed rowid lookup for rebuild update and delete; real SQLite query plans demonstrate bounded identity lookup with the former predicate as a negative control; update move delete and duplicate-id replacement retain exact search parity; old derived index versions are refused and rebuilt; the 100000-item explicit point-read scale control completes with its full corpus count
parent: pm-801d
resolution: Maintain FTS rows through indexed item rowid and migrate the derived index to version 5
expected_result: Rebuild update and deletion avoid unindexed FTS identity scans while preserving search parity
actual_result: Real SQLite query-plan negative control and update/delete/replacement tests pass; complete 100000-row cold scan finishes in 48.590 seconds
